A||||8||Hank is Here||Has anyone ever rolled or flipped a Fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||Hank is Here||01-14-2001||11:09 PM||||Really I have no reason for asking this except for coursity.<P>Has anyone rolled of flipped a Fiero, or seen the aftermath of one?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-14-2001||11:19 PM||||Rolling a Fiero is pretty difficult to do on solid ground (due to it's low center of gravity).  That said, I have seen the aftermath of a rolled Fiero.  There was a kid in high school who drove a new '87 Fiero GT (this was in 1987).  He drove it off the highway and overcorrected......he spun around and due to skidding on the soft shoulder rolled it several times.<P>At the time a loaded '87 GT was worth $14K+ so it was repaired.  They basically rebuilt this car frm the ground up.......they replaced about 1/3 of the frame (including the roof, of course).  I believe the total repair bill was in excess of $8000!<P>I discovered this 8 years ago when I wrecked my '88 GT and brought it into a local repair shop.  They had before, during and after pictures.  I'll see if they still have them and will see if I can scan them to my computer.<P>The car was a mess, but looked brand new again after they fixed it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||01-14-2001||11:21 PM||||The second last 1988 GT was flipped in Alaska.  I know because I delivered an airplane to Grand Cayman and the pilot that took posession owned it.  Apparantly he was a helicopter pilot working on some lodging site when a load of lumber got loose and rolled onto the road that he was driving on.  It pushed him and the Fiero over the ridge and that is why it rolled.  He got out of it without a scratch but the car was totalled. Too bad because that would be priceless now.  He's still a big Fiero buff in the Islands.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||onfire||01-14-2001||11:37 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/files/wreckage5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||01-14-2001||11:45 PM||||Shame. Those X-11 wheels look cool.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||01-14-2001||11:49 PM||||I was airborne, upside-down, and backwards at ~50mph in an '87 GT. It was one of the blue ones, too. Right now the car is sitting in my back yard holding spare parts. I may turn it into a convertible someday. With <I>large</I> roll bars.||||reg||1
