Z||000007||RaeQwan||01-15-2001||03:34 AM||||Ouch||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||01-15-2001||10:39 AM||||I was hanging out at a friends house<BR>(not the best neighborhood) when we heard some squeeling and crashing. My friends lived on a straightaway about 150 yards long, after the straight the road curved right, then left in order to meet up with the main road intersecting, which otherwise would have met at a 20 degree angle. <BR>When we got down to the "button hook" part, there was a white coupe flipped on it's side. Apparently it was stolen, and by the used hyperdermic found inside, the theives were flyin high.  The cops estimated they were going 50 mph when they hit the brakes and tried to make the turn and landed against a cyclone fence. The theives got away and there was suprisigly little damage to the coupe.<BR>||||reg||1
